  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Differentiated HIV Services for Key Populations in Malaysia - Malaysia (01-Jul-2022-30-Jun-2025)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaysia, HIV, Malaysian AIDS Council (MAC)This program has the following goals: To support the DHSKP program domestic funding with a view  adoption as the national mechanism for delivery of HIV services among KP.  To strengthen the capacity of civil society organistions and community-based organisations in HIV response towards achieving the 95-95-95 ending AIDS targets by 2030.. The objectives of this program are: To increase outreach coverage of MSM through physical outreach activities by 70000 clients (32% of the PSE) and 145000 (66% of the PSE) through online contacts..  To increase outreach coverage of SW through physical outreach activities by 8300 clients (38% of the PSE) and 8300 (38% of the PSE) through online contacts..  To increase outreach coverage of TG through physical outreach activities by 5600 clients (38% of the PSE) and 16800 (113% of the TGSW PSE, considering to also cover non-SW TG) through online contacts..  To increase the testing uptake to 95% of the total reached KPs over the grant period..  To increase the ART initiation by 90% of the total case detected within the grant period.</narrative>
  </description>
